  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hexanematichthys_sagor.htm",
      "html": "<p>Common name: Sagor catfish. Family: Ariidae. Size: 45 cm TL. The dorsal and pectoral spines are venomous on this species. IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hexanematichthys_sagor.htm",
      "html": "<p>Indo-West Pacific: Pakistan, India and Bangladesh east to Indonesia and Vietnam.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hexanematichthys_sagor.htm",
      "html": "<p>Found along the coastline, mainly around estuaries. Ascends into fresh water of the upper tidal zone. Occurs in the Mekong delta.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hexanematichthys_sagor.htm",
      "html": "<p>Feeds on invertebrates and small fishes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hexanematichthys_sagor.htm",
      "html": "<p>They carry the eggs in their mouths. Juveniles continue to hide in males' mouths for the first 2 months.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hexanematichthys_sagor.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: The genus name Hexanematichthys: Greek, exa = six + Greek, nema = filament + Greek, ichthys = fish. The species epithet sagor: Local Bengali name for this fish in India.</p>"
    }
  ],
